    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n494" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγημα</span></b> , τό, (from
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγω,</span> or perh. 
			Dor.
		 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥγημα;</span>
		
			Boeot.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγειμα</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			<u>BCH</u>
			18.534
		</span></i> (<span class="entity">Thisbe</span>)) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>anything led, division, corps</i> of an army, of the
			Lacedaemonians, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Lac.</u>
				11.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				13.6
			</span></i>: in the Macedonian army, <i>the Guard,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				5.65.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>An.</u>
				1.1.11
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ἱππέων τὸ ἄ.</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				4.24.1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν πεζῶν τὸ ἄ. 2.8.3; τῶν ἐλεφάντων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phylarch.
					1
				</span></i>
			: in the armies of the Ptolemies, etc., <i><span class="en">
				<u>PPetr.</u>
				3p.22
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Eum.</u>
				7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>Syr.</u>
				32
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ael.Dion.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				8
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βασιλικὸν ἄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					5.82.4
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> name of a
			district in the Heracleopolite nome, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PHib.</u>
				101.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PTeb.</u>
				3.38.4
			</span></i>.</div>
